.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-GPT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-gpt
.Nd write the GPT a Novi installation needs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar device
.Op Fl -esp-mib Ar n
.Op Fl -slot-mib Ar n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes one of two partition layouts and
.Sy destroys everything on Ar device .
It is called by
.Xr novi-install 1 ;
running it by hand is a way to lose a disk.
.Bl -tag -width "--slot-mib n"
.It Fl -esp-mib Ar n
Size of the EFI System partition.
Default 512, minimum 33 \(em a FAT32 filesystem needs the room.
.It Fl -slot-mib Ar n
Write the A/B layout instead, with two root slots of
.Ar n
MiB each.
Minimum 2048: the OS alone is about 800 MB.
.El
.Ss The two layouts
Default, two partitions:
.Bl -column -offset indent "2" "NOVI_ROOT_A" "Linux filesystem, the rest of the disk"
.It 1 Ta "" Ta EFI System, Fl -esp-mib No MiB
.It 2 Ta "" Ta Linux filesystem, the rest of the disk
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl -slot-mib Ar n :
.Bl -column -offset indent "2" "NOVI_ROOT_A" "Linux, the rest        shared state"
.It 1 Ta NOVI_ESP Ta EFI System, Fl -esp-mib No MiB
.It 2 Ta NOVI_ROOT_A Ta Linux, Ar n No MiB \(em root slot A
.It 3 Ta NOVI_ROOT_B Ta Linux, Ar n No MiB \(em root slot B, left empty
.It 4 Ta NOVI_STATE Ta Linux, the rest \(em shared state
.El
.Ss Why this exists, and why it writes only these two
BusyBox
fdisk(8)
can read a GPT and cannot create one, and the target has no sfdisk,
sgdisk or parted.
So this program is the missing half.
.Pp
It writes exactly these layouts
.Em on purpose :
a tool that can express every layout is a tool that can express the
wrong one.
The contract used to say one layout and now says two, which is a
change worth making as deliberately as the original rule was.
.Pp
An ESP on an MBR label was considered and rejected.
Plenty of firmware boots it, OVMF included \(em which is the problem:
it would pass here and fail on somebody's laptop.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It exits 2 on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-gpt /dev/vda --esp-mib 512
# novi-gpt /dev/vda --esp-mib 512 --slot-mib 4096
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-install 1 ,
.Xr novi-slot 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0008, RFC 0041.
.Sh CAVEATS
The two classic GPT mistakes are handled explicitly and are worth
knowing before editing this: type GUIDs are byte literals in GPT's
mixed-endian order, and the header CRC covers
.Va header_size
bytes with the CRC field zeroed, not the whole sector.
